<%# Redmine does not include a plugin's stylesheets on its own, so this partial
    emits the one link the plugin needs. The URL is not the same on every
    supported Redmine, and getting it wrong is a silent 404 (unstyled page,
    green CI):

    - Redmine 5.x copies assets/ into public/plugin_assets/<plugin_id>/ at boot,
      keeping the subdirectories. The file is then plain static content, so a
      static href is enough -- and safer than asking Sprockets to resolve a
      logical path that only exists because it was mirrored.
    - Redmine 6.0 replaced the copy with the asset pipeline (Propshaft since
      7.0): assets/ subdirectories are flattened under one prefix, the URL
      carries a content digest, and the file is only materialised by
      `assets:precompile` (which Redmine runs on boot when
      config.assets.redmine_detect_update is on, i.e. in production).
      stylesheet_link_tag is the only way to get that digested URL right.

    Redmine::Plugin#asset_prefix only exists from 6.0 on, which is exactly the
    boundary, so the version decides. %>
<% if Redmine::VERSION::MAJOR >= 6 %>
  <%= stylesheet_link_tag 'plugin_assets/redmine_status_flow/redmine_status_flow', media: 'all' %>
<% else %>
  <%= tag.link rel: 'stylesheet', media: 'all',
               href: "#{Redmine::Utils.relative_url_root}/plugin_assets/redmine_status_flow/stylesheets/redmine_status_flow.css" %>
<% end %>
